{"id": "reczz28LeeYH4bwm", "order": 1, "images": ["/media/e84145a803a61bf07c9bec1e.jpeg", "/media/151d72520a062dd8fd34c572.jpeg", "/media/61f19b34fb126c46c20404b7.jpeg", "/media/ec72cacb666f71b775ba3bd2.jpeg", "/media/74bea616360ba1388a4ec9d6.jpeg", "/media/95fa3f5266003122812e85cb.jpg", "/media/58e9ffa098ea4d20dd7644d8.jpg", "/media/a51f464388af8c2a3e5e07cf.jpg", "/media/aa95b71447a97ca0cdebc993.png"], "name": "Well and Truly", "originalName": "Well and Truly", "termName": "清透", "author": "Roni Horn", "year": "2009–2010", "medium": "铸造玻璃", "collection": "", "caption": "", "why": "你以为那是一池水，其实是重达数百公斤的玻璃。", "whyLong": "十块淡蓝、青绿、灰白色的实心玻璃静静放在地面，顶部却像盛满了一池水。光线在玻璃内部散开，厚重的固体看起来几乎没有重量。\n\n想想一杯澄澈的水：你能看见水杯底部，又能从光线的折射、水面的反光中意识到水的存在。清透最微妙的美，恰恰是介于「看得见」和「看不见」之间——这十块玻璃把这句话做成了实物。", "scene": "", "detail": "", "method": "", "twist": "", "absence": "", "extra": "", "official": "https://lesoeuvres.pinaultcollection.com/en/artwork/well-and-truly"}